meta {
  name: Reuse a key with a different request
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/loans
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "bookId": "{{bookId}}",
    "userId": "{{userId}}",
    "loanDays": 30
  }
}

docs {
  409, and meant to be.

  The same key as the two requests above, but loanDays is 30 rather than 14 - so this is a
  different request wearing a used key. Replaying the first response would tell the caller a
  loan was made that they did not ask for, so it is refused instead.

  The comparison is a SHA-256 of the request's values rather than of its raw bytes, so
  reformatting the JSON or reordering its properties does not make an honest retry look like
  this. Only a value the API would have acted on differently does.
}
